tasks.statement:
`ctx.get_parameter_source(name)` returns `None` when it is called while the parameter is still being processed: inside a custom `ParamType.convert()` and inside the callback of an eager option. It used to return the real source in earlier releases.

Reproduce:

```python
import click

class Source(click.ParamType):
    name = "source"
    def convert(self, value, param, ctx):
        return {"value": value, "source": ctx.get_parameter_source(param.name)}

@click.command()
@click.option("--default", type=Source(), default="/tmp/file")
def cli(default):
    click.echo(default)
```

Running `cli` with no arguments prints `'source': None`; expected `ParameterSource.DEFAULT` (and `ParameterSource.COMMANDLINE` when `--default x` is passed). Likewise, an eager boolean flag option with a callback must see `DEFAULT` or `COMMANDLINE` from `ctx.get_parameter_source(param.name)` inside the callback. The source reported after parsing has finished must stay correct, including when several options share one parameter name.
